<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!-- The strip along the bottom of the player that never accepts a touch,
         not even while the overlay has been lifted.

         What it covers is everything below YouTube's seek bar. The embed draws
         its control row inset from the bottom edge, so under the bar there is
         a band that belongs to nothing useful — and a scrub that drifts
         downward off the bar lands there, on whatever the player puts under
         it, or on the system's back/home gesture.

         This is now only the STARTING value. The player is a cross-origin
         iframe, so its DOM cannot be read and there is no way to ask where the
         bar is — but there is a way to look, and PlayerActivity does: on the
         first pause it draws the bottom of the player and finds the seek bar
         in the pixels (see Chrome.kt), then sets this height from what it
         found. What is left here is the fallback for before that has happened
         and for when it fails.

         Erring small on purpose: too tall and it eats the seek bar, which is
         the one control the reveal exists to reach. -->
    <dimen name="player_bottom_block">16dp</dimen>

    <!-- How much of the space under the seek bar is left reachable once the
         bar has been found.

         The drawn bar is thin — nine pixels on the frame this was measured
         from, under 4dp — and a thumb aiming for it lands around it rather
         than on it. Everything ABOVE the bar is reachable already, so this
         only has to cover fingers that land low. Blocking flush to the line
         would make the one control the reveal exists to reach the one control
         nobody can hit.

         Twenty rather than more because it has to fit: on that frame there
         were 217 pixels under the bar and the row of ways out of the app —
         share, "More videos", the YouTube wordmark — began 58 of them down.
         Widening this much further starts uncovering that row. -->
    <dimen name="player_seek_touch_margin">20dp</dimen>

</resources>
